 ── Pick where it goes · s  squash, choosing where into ─────────────────────── 
 Moves the revision's changes into another one you pick, its parent by default, 
 and drops the revision once it is empty. -i chooses the hunks; -o/-A/-B make a 
 new commit.                                                                    
 runs   jj squash --from <rev> --into <dest>                                    
 flags  -t into · -o into a new commit onto · -A into a new commit after · -B   
        into a new commit before · -u keep the destination's message · -m write 
        the message · -k keep the source if it empties · -i choose hunks        
 also   A absorb S split                                                        
